1
00:05:38,823 --> 00:05:44,823
You'll live the adventure... You'll love its heroes.

2
00:11:17,647 --> 00:11:23,647
The Ewok Adventure is a adventure, family, fantasy film directed by John Korty.

3
00:16:56,470 --> 00:17:02,470
Wicket the Ewok and his friends agree to help two shipwrecked human
children, Mace and Cindel, on a quest to find their parents.

4
00:22:35,294 --> 00:22:41,294
Mace Towani, played by Eric Walker.

5
00:28:14,117 --> 00:28:20,117
Wicket W. Warrick, played by Warwick Davis.

6
00:33:52,941 --> 00:33:58,941
Catarine Towani, played by Fionnula Flanagan.

7
00:39:31,764 --> 00:39:37,764
Jeremitt Towani, played by Guy Boyd.

8
00:45:10,588 --> 00:45:16,588
Cindel Towani, played by Aubree Miller.

9
00:50:49,411 --> 00:50:55,411
Deej Warrick, played by Daniel Frishman.

10
00:56:28,235 --> 00:56:34,235
The Ewok Adventure is a 1984 American television
film based in the Star Wars universe.

11
01:02:07,058 --> 01:02:13,058
It takes place on the moon of Endor, and features the Ewoks, who help two
young human siblings as they try to locate their parents.

12
01:07:45,882 --> 01:07:51,882
The film premiered on November 25, 1984 on ABC.

13
01:13:24,705 --> 01:13:30,705
The film was given a limited international theatrical run, for which
it was retitled Caravan of Courage: An Ewok Adventure.

14
01:19:03,529 --> 01:19:09,529
It was followed by a sequel, Ewoks: The Battle for Endor, in 1985.

15
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The film explores themes of rescue, space marine,
monster, parent child relationship, magic.

16
01:30:21,176 --> 01:30:27,176
The tone is thought_provoking.
